"fullPath":"/news/join-our-volunteer-reviewer-pool","imagePath":"https://agency.icjia-api.cloud/uploads/E74iqlq_WQAE_5pq_M_7a2ccba5a4.jpg","displayCategory":"news","contentType":"news","publicationDate":"2021-08-03","tagsAlt":[{"title":"Funding","slug":"funding"},{"title":"Volunteer","slug":"volunteer"}]},{"id":"18","title":"ICJIA Celebrates Juneteenth: A Message from the Acting Executive Director","created_at":"2021-08-04T13:33:07.831Z","updated_at":"2021-08-04T18:08:49.140Z","slug":"icjia-celebrates-juneteenth","summary":"Today ICJIA celebrates Juneteenth in commemoration of the Emancipation Proclamation signed in 1863 and for the freedom that finally came for those still enslaved by the confederates on June 19, 1865. On that day, some 2,000 Union troops arrived in Galveston Bay, Texas. The army announced that the more than 250,000 enslaved Black people in the state were free by executive decree. Upon their freedom, newly freed Black people in Texas organized a Jubilee Day for the next year and in decades to come, this day came to be known as “Juneteenth.” Juneteenth marks our country’s second Independence Day.","category":"news","searchMeta":"delrice adams executive director","published_at":"2021-08-04T13:33:10.194Z","dateOverride":"2021-06-18","tags":[],"splash":{"name":"Juneteenth 2021.jpg","caption":"","alternativeText":"","url":"/uploads/Juneteenth_2021_c8dafaf133.jpg","formats":{"thumbnail":{"name":"thumbnail_Juneteenth 2021.jpg","hash":"thumbnail_Juneteenth_2021_c8dafaf133","ext":".jpg","mime":"image/jpeg","width":245,"height":111,"size":9.23,"path":null,"url":"/uploads/thumbnail_Juneteenth_2021_c8dafaf133.jpg"},"large":{"name":"large_Juneteenth 2021.jpg","hash":"large_Juneteenth_2021_c8dafaf133","ext":".jpg","mime":"image/jpeg","width":1000,"height":455,"size":68.2,"path":null,"url":"/uploads/large_Juneteenth_2021_c8dafaf133.jpg"},"medium":{"name":"medium_Juneteenth 2021.jpg","hash":"medium_Juneteenth_2021_c8dafaf133","ext":".jpg","mime":"image/jpeg","widt